    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Toni Preckwinkle has served as Cook County Board President since 2010 and oversees the county's public health system, court system and annual budget. She is also president of the Forest Preserves of Cook County. She previously taught high school history and served as alderman of Chicago's 4th Ward for 19 years.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Toni Preckwinkle has served as Cook County Board President since 2010 and oversees the county's public health system, court system and annual budget.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She is also president of the Forest Preserves of Cook County.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "She previously taught high school history and served as alderman of Chicago's 4th Ward for 19 years.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "As Cook County Board President, she lobbied for laws that raised the age for detention in adult jail from 17 to 18 and narrowed the crimes for which juveniles can be tried as adults. Her campaign says she has expanded access to health care for 350,000 people. In October 2026, she announced an $8 million county investment to help south suburban communities clean up from severe summer storms. As an alderman, she sponsored the living wage and affordable housing ordinance.",
